<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 733 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 733 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of November 7 raised nearly 733 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 1,058 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 138 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.56 (14.61)	  114.4 (93.2)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.89 (16.92)	  144.2 (323.7)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.75 (17.78)	  105.4 (104.3)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.58 (21.62)	  368.9 (536.5)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,555.5 to the dollar on Monday from 1,556 a week earlier and 1,602 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
